import JobsWorkbenchDemo from './JobsWorkbenchDemo.astro';
---
<section class="ls-container ls-jobs-episode" id="jobs-workbench" aria-labelledby="jobs-workbench-title">
  <div class="ls-jobs-intro">
    <div><p class="ls-eyebrow">JOBS ARE PART OF THE DOCUMENT</p>
      <h2 id="jobs-workbench-title">SEE THE WORK.<br/><span class="ls-stroke">MAKE THE CALL.</span></h2></div>
    <div class="ls-episode-dek"><p>A research brief can carry its own Jobs. Inspect the saved Job, trace its declared inputs and outputs, and run a sample update.</p>
    <p>When the page changes, review one part at a time. Keep records your decision. Revert restores that part. Later leaves it applied, ready for your return.</p></div>
  </div>
  <JobsWorkbenchDemo />
  <p class="ls-jobs-caption">Try the walkthrough: add interview I12, run Research Refresh, then inspect the changed table and chart. Sample data from the included Customer Research documents.</p>
</section>
